cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "egernia: an IVOA TAP 1.1 server for the SKA Regional Centre Network"
message: "If you use this software in published work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Delli Veneri"
    given-names: "Michele"
    affiliation: "SKA Observatory"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ska-telescope/egernia"
url: "https://ska-telescope.github.io/egernia/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An IVOA Table Access Protocol (TAP) 1.1 server implemented in Python as two
  stateless microservices over a single PostgreSQL database. ADQL queries are
  translated to PostgreSQL with pg_sphere geometry, executed under a read-only
  role with a statement timeout, and streamed as VOTable, CSV, TSV, JSON,
  Parquet or Arrow. Asynchronous queries follow UWS 1.1, using the database
  itself as the job queue. Metadata domains bind pydantic model packages to
  generated SQL schemas registered in TAP_SCHEMA, so ingested metadata is
  queryable through ordinary ADQL.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - virtual observatory
  - IVOA
  - TAP
  - ADQL
  - SKA
  - PostgreSQL
